2. PROHIBITION OF COMMERCIAL USE

Commercial Use is prohibited for all parties, including the original author.
"Commercial Use" means any use primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage or monetary compensation. This includes, but is not
limited to:

- Selling, licensing, or sublicensing the work for a fee
- Incorporating the work into a commercial product or service
- Using the work to generate revenue directly or indirectly
- Using the work to train or develop commercial AI, machine learning models,
  or large language models
- Using the work in any automated service, SaaS platform, or cloud offering
  that generates revenue
- Using the work internally within a for-profit organization to support
  revenue-generating activities
- Charging for access to the work, including paywalled documentation, paid
  support, or training services centered on the work
- Monetizing the work through advertising or sponsorships
- Bundling the work with paid products or services
- Data monetization derived from the work

The following are NOT considered Commercial Use:

- Personal learning and education
- Academic research at non-profit institutions
- Open source contributions without monetary compensation
- Content creation (teaching, streaming, educational materials) even if it
  generates incidental revenue
- Charging only for the actual, verifiable cost of physical distribution media

If a use has both commercial and non-commercial purposes, it shall be deemed
Commercial Use if the primary purpose at the time of use is commercial.

3. PROHIBITION OF MONETIZATION OF THE WORK

The work itself may not be used for monetization in any form. This includes,
but is not limited to:

- Commercial sale of the work
- Paid services centered on the work
- Advertising displayed alongside or within the work
- Donations, sponsorships, or platform incentives associated with the work
- Revenue sharing derived from the work
- Incorporating the work into any product or service operated for profit

Platform-automated advertising and platform-unilateral incentives do not
constitute a violation by the adopter, provided that the adopter actively
disables such functions where possible. The adopter's other commercial
activities, unrelated to the work, are not restricted. The adopter's commercial
status does not constitute a violation.

Pages displaying or distributing the work may not feature donations,
sponsorships, or advertising.

